[2026-05-10] [Public Launch] — Decision: Hybrid persona model (user-configured with preset shortcuts). Rejected: generic/stripped AI only. Because: the app's value comes from personalized AI voice; presets lower the onboarding bar without sacrificing quality.
[2026-05-10] [Public Launch] — Decision: Free tier (1 sort/week) + BYOK (unlimited, user's own key). Rejected: fully hosted paid-only, fully free. Because: BYOK removes cost risk for power users; free tier lets newbies experience the value before committing.
[2026-05-10] [Public Launch] — Decision: No Stripe/payments in v1. Rejected: build billing before launch. Because: validate with real users before building payment infrastructure; ship fast and learn.
[2026-05-10] [Public Launch] — Decision: Supabase for user data (personas, encrypted BYOK keys, usage tracking). Rejected: session/cookie-only storage. Because: cookies can't enforce server-side rate limits and don't persist across devices.
[2026-05-10] [Public Launch] — Decision: Owner email bypass via env var preserves Dr. K clinic context unchanged. Rejected: migrating clinic context into the persona system. Because: existing behavior must not regress for Katelyn while multi-user is being built.
[2026-05-28] [Email Party] — Decision: Two modes only — Zen and Party. Rejected: Neon Disco + Monastery as separate modes. Because: start with the core emotional contrast (calm vs. energized) before adding more modes; simpler toggle is less cognitive load.
[2026-05-28] [Email Party] — Decision: Mode is a session intention set at the Quote Gate, switchable mid-session via header toggle. Rejected: permanent preference setting in InstructionsPanel. Because: user's energy varies day-to-day; the gate makes the choice feel intentional, not administrative.
[2026-05-28] [Email Party] — Decision: Zen mode = full inbox visible with collapsible categories and muted palette. Rejected: Zen mode hides newsletters/filters to urgent-only. Because: filtering is unreliable; user still wants access to all emails but with calm presentation.
[2026-05-28] [Email Party] — Decision: Mindful Purge uses existing email data (actionFlag + age) — no new API call. Rejected: new Claude call to identify purgeable emails. Because: actionFlag="read" + 7-day age is a reliable enough heuristic; avoids latency and cost.
[2026-05-28] [Email Party] — Decision: Zen Summary (Challenge/Ask/Vibe) deferred to v2. Rejected: include in v1. Because: requires a new Claude call per opened email; adds latency and cost; ship the mode system first.
